  { number := 73, text := "## 3. Definitions" },
  { number := 74, text := "" },
  { number := 75, text := "### 3.1 SSSSS" },
  { number := 76, text := "" },
  { number := 77, text := "The Surmount Systems Smart Symbolic Supercompiler specified by this document. The short name is the five ASCII letters S, S, S, S, S." },
  { number := 78, text := "" },
  { number := 79, text := "### 3.2 Language run" },
  { number := 80, text := "" },
  { number := 81, text := "A LanguageID together with an ordered list of WordID values in that language. A language run is the unit of sequential encoding after tokens are split and vocabulary is assigned." },
  { number := 82, text := "" },
  { number := 83, text := "### 3.3 LanguageID" },
  { number := 84, text := "" },
  { number := 85, text := "A 64 bit sequential integer that names a language. It is assigned from the unused LanguageID space in increasing order. It is not a hash of a language name. It is not a Unicode code point used as the primary key. The LanguageID space has capacity `2^64`." },
  { number := 86, text := "" },
  { number := 87, text := "### 3.4 WordID" },
  { number := 88, text := "" },
  { number := 89, text := "A 64 bit sequential integer that names a word or other vocabulary atom in one language. For each LanguageID, WordID values are assigned from that language's unused WordID space in increasing order. A WordID is not a hash of surface text. It is not a Unicode code point used as the primary key. Each language has WordID capacity `2^64`. Combined capacity is `2^64` languages times `2^64` WordIDs." },
  { number := 90, text := "" },
  { number := 91, text := "### 3.5 Primary identity" },
  { number := 92, text := "" },
  { number := 93, text := "The stored identifier used to look up, persist, and relate a language or a word. In this specification primary identity is sequential LanguageID and sequential WordID. Hashing MUST NOT be primary identity (Clause 4.1)." },
  { number := 94, text := "" },
  { number := 95, text := "### 3.6 Rosetta layer" },
  { number := 96, text := "" },
  { number := 97, text := "The set of accepted Rosetta relations that relate vocabulary atoms across languages so translation and other correspondences can be expressed as integer edges rather than as hashed surface strings." },
  { number := 98, text := "" },
  { number := 99, text := "### 3.7 Rosetta relation" },
  { number := 100, text := "" },
  { number := 101, text := "A record with six fields: LanguageID of language A, WordID in language A, RelationType, LanguageID of language B, WordID in language B, and Provenance." },
  { number := 102, text := "" },
  { number := 103, text := "### 3.8 RelationType" },
  { number := 104, text := "" },
  { number := 105, text := "A name for the correspondence a Rosetta relation asserts. This specification does not freeze a closed list of kinds. Examples include translation, synonymy, and hypernymy. Additional kinds MAY be defined by the implementation. A RelationType MUST be present on every Rosetta relation." },
  { number := 106, text := "" },
  { number := 107, text := "### 3.9 Provenance" },
  { number := 108, text := "" },
  { number := 109, text := "The origin tag on a Rosetta relation. It MUST be one of the following:" },
  { number := 110, text := "" },
  { number := 111, text := "1. `neural-proposed`" },
  { number := 112, text := "2. `human-confirmed`" },
  { number := 113, text := "3. `Lean-proven`" },
  { number := 114, text := "" },
  { number := 115, text := "### 3.10 Vocabulary" },
  { number := 116, text := "" },
  { number := 117, text := "The assigned mapping from surface tokens in a language to sequential WordID values for that LanguageID, together with the assigned LanguageID values themselves." },
  { number := 118, text := "" },
  { number := 119, text := "### 3.11 Intermediate representation" },
  { number := 120, text := "" },
  { number := 121, text := "The pipeline's working form after ingest: language runs plus accepted Rosetta relations. This document MAY abbreviate that form as IR after this definition." },
  { number := 122, text := "" },
  { number := 123, text := "### 3.12 Neural proposal" },
  { number := 124, text := "" },
  { number := 125, text := "A suggested vocabulary assignment or Rosetta relation produced by a neural method. Neural proposals are optional (Clause 4.4). They are not primary identity." },
  { number := 126, text := "" },
  { number := 127, text := "### 3.13 Natural language translation" },
  { number := 128, text := "" },
  { number := 129, text := "Best effort translation among written natural languages. It is optional (Clause 4.5). It is not a substitute for deterministic programming language translation." },
  { number := 130, text := "" },
  { number := 131, text := "### 3.14 High confidence mark" },
  { number := 132, text := "" },
  { number := 133, text := "A named mark an implementation attaches to a natural language translation to mean the implementation treats that translation as high confidence. The threshold and name are defined by the implementation. Absence of Lean proof and absence of a high confidence mark requires the translation to be marked provisional (Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 134, text := "" },
  { number := 135, text := "### 3.15 Lean Machine substrate" },
  { number := 136, text := "" },
  { number := 137, text := "The Lean Machine formalization layer named in Scope as a substrate of SSSSS. Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`. That document is specification 0013." },
  { number := 138, text := "" },
  { number := 139, text := "### 3.16 Systems Lean" },
  { number := 140, text := "" },
  { number := 141, text := "The language specified in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md): Lean 4 with linear and affine ownership and Quantitative Type Theory multiplicities 0, 1, and omega." },
  { number := 142, text := "" },
  { number := 143, text := "### 3.17 Slake" },
  { number := 144, text := "" },
  { number := 145, text := "The compiler specified in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md): the compiler written in Systems Lean that emits freestanding products." },
  { number := 146, text := "" },
  { number := 147, text := "### 3.18 beastdb" },
  { number := 148, text := "" },
  { number := 149, text := "The durable ordered store specified in [0003_beastdb.md](0003_beastdb.md). The product name is the lowercase form beastdb." },
  { number := 150, text := "" },
  { number := 151, text := "### 3.19 Requirement keywords" },
  { number := 152, text := "" },
  { number := 153, text := "The key words MUST, MUST NOT, REQUIRED, SHALL, SHALL NOT, SHOULD, SHOULD NOT, RECOMMENDED, MAY, and OPTIONAL in this document are to be interpreted as described in RFC 2119." },
  { number := 154, text := "" },
  { number := 155, text := "### 3.20 CompCert verified compilation" },
  { number := 156, text := "" },
  { number := 157, text := "Compilation of the freestanding C emit by CompCert (`ccomp`) such that the generated assembly is the CompCert verified compilation of that C, as defined in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) Clause 3.9." },
  { number := 158, text := "" },
  { number := 159, text := "### 3.21 Slake that fully typechecks" },
  { number := 160, text := "" },
  { number := 161, text := "A bootstrapped Slake compiler that typechecks the Systems Lean and Slake sources it is bootstrapped from, including theorems, as defined in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) Clause 3.10. A named subset of modules is not enough. Emitting freestanding C without that typecheck is not enough." },
  { number := 162, text := "" },
  { number := 163, text := "### 3.22 Named hole" },
  { number := 164, text := "" },
  { number := 165, text := "An explicit, tracked absence of a target WordID when emit cannot find an accepted Rosetta relation for a source WordID under the target LanguageID." },
  { number := 166, text := "" },
  { number := 167, text := "### 3.23 Harness" },
  { number := 168, text := "" },
  { number := 169, text := "The SSSSS product environment that exposes tools, translation, and calls that change those tools. This document does not claim a harness is implemented." },
  { number := 170, text := "" },
  { number := 171, text := "### 3.24 Symbolic interface" },
  { number := 172, text := "" },
  { number := 173, text := "Lean programs in the harness that perform a tool or translation action only when proved consistent, constructive, and deterministic, using sequential LanguageID and WordID and accepted Rosetta relations." },
  { number := 174, text := "" },
  { number := 175, text := "### 3.25 Neural path" },
  { number := 176, text := "" },
  { number := 177, text := "A neural model used only when the symbolic interface cannot complete that action." },
  { number := 178, text := "" },
  { number := 179, text := "### 3.26 Tool improvement call" },
  { number := 180, text := "" },
  { number := 181, text := "A call native to the harness that changes a tool so a later symbolic path can succeed. That is Recursive Self Improvement of tools as specified in `0006_RSI.md`." },
  { number := 182, text := "" },
  { number := 183, text := "### 3.27 Neurosymbolic combination" },
  { number := 184, text := "" },
  { number := 185, text := "The pairing of the symbolic interface and the neural path so work is not repeated: do not spend neural work on an action the symbolic interface can already perform." },
  { number := 186, text := "" },
  { number := 187, text := "## 4. Core requirements" },
  { number := 188, text := "" },
  { number := 189, text := "### 4.1 Representation" },
  { number := 190, text := "" },
  { number := 191, text := "1. A conforming SSSSS MUST encode programs as language runs (Clause 3.2)." },
  { number := 192, text := "2. In a serialized stream of language runs, a LanguageID prefix MUST appear when the language of the following WordID sequence differs from the previous language in that stream, including at the start of the stream. A LanguageID prefix MUST NOT be repeated before every WordID when the language has not changed." },
  { number := 193, text := "3. LanguageID values MUST be 64 bit sequential integers (Clause 3.3)." },
  { number := 194, text := "4. WordID values MUST be 64 bit sequential integers assigned per LanguageID (Clause 3.4)." },
  { number := 195, text := "5. Hashing MUST NOT be primary identity for languages or words (Clause 3.5). A digest of surface text MAY exist as an auxiliary index. An auxiliary index MUST NOT replace sequential LanguageID or sequential WordID as the stored identifier used for lookup, persistence, or Rosetta relations." },
  { number := 196, text := "6. Combined identifier capacity MUST be `2^64` languages times `2^64` WordIDs." },
  { number := 197, text := "7. Items 1 through 6 are requirements. This document does not claim an encoder, a vocabulary store, or sequential WordID assignment is implemented." },
  { number := 198, text := "" },
  { number := 199, text := "### 4.2 Rosetta" },
  { number := 200, text := "" },
  { number := 201, text := "1. A conforming SSSSS MUST represent each accepted cross language correspondence as a Rosetta relation (Clause 3.7) with fields LanguageID of language A, WordID in language A, RelationType, LanguageID of language B, WordID in language B, and Provenance." },
  { number := 202, text := "2. Provenance MUST be `neural-proposed`, `human-confirmed`, or `Lean-proven` (Clause 3.9)." },
  { number := 203, text := "3. A RelationType MUST be present (Clause 3.8)." },
  { number := 204, text := "4. Rosetta relations MUST use sequential LanguageID and WordID values. They MUST NOT use hashing as primary identity of either endpoint." },
  { number := 205, text := "5. Items 1 through 4 are requirements. This document does not claim a Rosetta store is implemented." },
  { number := 206, text := "" },
  { number := 207, text := "### 4.3 Pipeline" },
  { number := 208, text := "" },
  { number := 209, text := "1. Given the same vocabulary and the same set of accepted Rosetta relations, the pipeline MUST be deterministic: the same source token sequence and the same target LanguageID MUST produce the same emit." },
  { number := 210, text := "2. The pipeline MUST ingest source text and tokenize it into candidate surface tokens." },
  { number := 211, text := "3. The pipeline MUST look up each token in the vocabulary for the current LanguageID, or insert a new sequential WordID when the token is new in that language." },
  { number := 212, text := "4. The intermediate representation MUST be language runs plus accepted Rosetta relations (Clause 3.11)." },
  { number := 213, text := "5. The pipeline MAY formalize fragments of that intermediate representation into Systems Lean as specified in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md)." },
  { number := 214, text := "6. Emit MUST map source WordID values to target WordID values by inverse lookup under the target LanguageID through accepted Rosetta relations." },
  { number := 215, text := "7. If no accepted Rosetta relation provides a target WordID, a conforming implementation MUST NOT invent hashing as the identity of that token. It MUST either fail the translation of that token or emit a named hole (Clause 3.22). Choosing between those two outcomes is defined by the implementation." },
  { number := 216, text := "8. Items 1 through 4, 6, and 7 are requirements. Item 5 is optional. This document does not claim a pipeline is implemented." },
  { number := 217, text := "" },
  { number := 218, text := "### 4.4 Neural proposals" },
  { number := 219, text := "" },
  { number := 220, text := "1. A conforming SSSSS MAY accept neural proposals (Clause 3.12)." },
  { number := 221, text := "2. A neural proposal MUST be reduced to sequential integers (LanguageID, WordID, and any other integers this specification uses as identity) before it is accepted into the vocabulary or the Rosetta relation set." },
  { number := 222, text := "3. A neural proposal that has not been reduced to sequential integers MUST NOT be accepted." },
  { number := 223, text := "4. When a neural proposal would become authoritative for semantics or for behavior that is safety critical, it SHOULD be Lean proven before it is treated as authoritative. That SHOULD is not a substitute for item 2." },
  { number := 224, text := "5. Items 2 and 3 are requirements. Item 1 is optional. Item 4 is a SHOULD. This document does not claim a neural proposer exists." },
  { number := 225, text := "" },
  { number := 226, text := "### 4.5 Natural language translation" },
  { number := 227, text := "" },
  { number := 228, text := "1. A conforming SSSSS MAY offer written natural language translation (Clause 3.13)." },
  { number := 229, text := "2. Natural language translation is best effort and is not required to be deterministic in the sense of Clause 4.3 item 1." },
  { number := 230, text := "3. A natural language translation MUST be marked provisional unless it is Lean proven or it carries a high confidence mark (Clause 3.14)." },
  { number := 231, text := "4. Best effort natural language translation MUST NOT be treated as a substitute for deterministic programming language translation (Clause 4.3)." },
  { number := 232, text := "5. Items 3 and 4 are requirements when natural language translation is offered. Item 1 is optional. This document does not claim a natural language translator exists." },
  { number := 233, text := "" },
  { number := 234, text := "### 4.6 Durable state, Systems Lean core, and 0002 validation" },
  { number := 235, text := "" },
  { number := 236, text := "1. Durable SSSSS state MUST be stored in beastdb as specified in [0003_beastdb.md](0003_beastdb.md)." },
  { number := 237, text := "2. The core of SSSSS MUST be implemented in Systems Lean as specified in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md)." },
  { number := 238, text := "3. SSSSS components that are safety critical, SSSSS components that run in environments with tight resources, and SSSSS components that are freestanding MUST be able to target the freestanding Slake path in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md). Those components MUST contain no managed Lean runtime and MUST NOT perform garbage collection on the freestanding product wire." },
  { number := 239, text := "4. CompCert verified compilation (Clause 3.20) is a REQUIRED core validation step for the freestanding C emit of the components named in item 3, as defined in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) Clause 3.9 and as required by that document's Clause 4.2 item 6. Naming a residual MUST NOT substitute for this step. This document does not claim CompCert is pinned under this specifications repository's `ref/`." },
  { number := 240, text := "5. Bootstrapping a Slake compiler that fully typechecks (Clause 3.21) is a REQUIRED core validation step for those same components, as required by [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) Clause 4.2 item 7. A named subset of modules is not enough. Naming a residual MUST NOT substitute for this step. A claim that the freestanding product hosts itself from generated C is a distinct claim and does not satisfy this step by itself." },
  { number := 241, text := "6. Residual honesty as defined in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) remains required for the freestanding product wire. Residual honesty MUST NOT replace items 4 and 5." },
  { number := 242, text := "7. Items 1 through 6 are requirements. This document does not claim an SSSSS backed by beastdb, an SSSSS core built by Slake, CompCert validation of an SSSSS emit, or a Slake bootstrap that fully typechecks for SSSSS is implemented." },
  { number := 243, text := "" },
  { number := 244, text := "### 4.7 Neurosymbolic integration" },
  { number := 245, text := "" },
  { number := 246, text := "This clause specifies how a claimed SSSSS harness combines the symbolic interface (Clause 3.24) and the neural path (Clause 3.25). It is not a one line pointer. Translation that only maps language runs, without a harness, is unchanged by this clause. Clause 4.4 neural proposals stay optional and distinct from this interface." },
  { number := 247, text := "" },
  { number := 248, text := "A neurosymbolic combination (Clause 3.27) is the rule that work is not repeated: the product MUST NOT spend neural work on an action the symbolic interface can already perform." },
  { number := 249, text := "" },
  { number := 250, text := "When a product claims the neurosymbolic harness interface, all of the following MUST hold:" },
  { number := 251, text := "" },
  { number := 252, text := "1. The product MUST expose the symbolic interface in the harness as an alternative deterministic interface for tool and translation actions." },
  { number := 253, text := "2. That symbolic interface MUST be implemented in Systems Lean as specified in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md)." },
  { number := 254, text := "3. Recipe lookup and emit MUST be deterministic given the same vocabulary and the same set of accepted Rosetta relations. The same source, the same target LanguageID, the same vocabulary, and the same accepted Rosetta set MUST produce the same emit (Clause 4.3 item 1)." },
  { number := 255, text := "4. The neural path MUST NOT be used for an action the symbolic interface can complete." },
  { number := 256, text := "5. When the symbolic interface cannot complete an action, the product MAY use the neural path to improve tools through calls native to the harness (Clause 3.26). Those improvements MUST be reduced to sequential integers before they are accepted, the same reduction as Clause 4.4 items 2 and 3." },
  { number := 257, text := "6. Training a model, or further training of a model, MUST NOT substitute for tool improvement inside the harness. This document MUST NOT invent a training cost number unless that number is cited with a markdown link and an access date. Prefer qualitative English about cost." },
  { number := 258, text := "7. Neural proposals under Clause 4.4 remain optional and distinct. Accepting a neural proposal under Clause 4.4 is not by itself a claim of this harness interface." },
  { number := 259, text := "" },
  { number := 260, text := "Items 1 through 6 are requirements if and only if the product claims the neurosymbolic harness interface. Item 7 keeps Clause 4.4 optional when that claim is absent." },
  { number := 261, text := "" },
  { number := 262, text := "This document does not claim that a neurosymbolic harness is implemented. The integration is specified here. It is not a shipped product." },
  { number := 263, text := "" },
  { number := 264, text := "#### 4.7.1 Other wires (informative)" },
  { number := 265, text := "" },
  { number := 266, text := "This subsection is informative. Model Context Protocol and Agent Client Protocol MAY be named as other wires that a product uses next to this interface. This specification does not forbid those wires. This specification does not require those wires." },
  { number := 267, text := "" },
  { number := 268, text := "## 5. Conformance" },
  { number := 269, text := "" },
  { number := 270, text := "An SSSSS implementation conforms to this specification if and only if all of the following hold:" },
  { number := 271, text := "" },
  { number := 272, text := "1. It encodes programs as language runs, emits a LanguageID prefix only when the language changes (including at stream start), uses 64 bit sequential LanguageID and per language sequential WordID values, does not use hashing as primary identity, and provides combined capacity `2^64` languages times `2^64` WordIDs (Clause 4.1)." },
  { number := 273, text := "2. It represents accepted cross language correspondences as Rosetta relations with RelationType and provenance `neural-proposed`, `human-confirmed`, or `Lean-proven`, using sequential LanguageID and WordID at both endpoints (Clause 4.2)." },
  { number := 274, text := "3. Given the same vocabulary and the same accepted Rosetta relation set, its pipeline is deterministic; it ingests and tokenizes, looks up or inserts sequential WordIDs, uses language runs plus Rosetta relations as intermediate representation, emits by inverse WordID lookup under the target LanguageID, and on a missing mapping fails that token or emits a named hole without inventing hash identity (Clause 4.3 items 1 through 4, 6, and 7). Formalizing fragments into Systems Lean (Clause 4.3 item 5) is not required." },
  { number := 275, text := "4. Every accepted neural proposal has been reduced to sequential integers (Clause 4.4 items 2 and 3). When natural language translation is offered, each such translation is marked provisional unless it is Lean proven or carries a high confidence mark, and natural language translation is not treated as a substitute for deterministic programming language translation (Clause 4.5). Neural proposals and natural language translation MAY be absent." },
  { number := 276, text := "5. Durable state is stored in beastdb (Clause 4.6 item 1). The core is implemented in Systems Lean (Clause 4.6 item 2). SSSSS components that are safety critical, that run in environments with tight resources, and that are freestanding target the freestanding Slake path without managed Lean runtime or garbage collection, CompCert verified compilation of their freestanding C emit has been performed, and a bootstrapped Slake fully typechecks the Systems Lean and Slake sources it is bootstrapped from (Clause 4.6 items 3 through 6). A named residual MUST NOT substitute for CompCert verified compilation or for the bootstrap typecheck." },
  { number := 277, text := "6. If and only if the product claims the neurosymbolic harness interface, Clause 4.7 items 1 through 6 hold: the symbolic interface is exposed in the harness as an alternative deterministic interface, that interface is implemented in Systems Lean, recipe lookup and emit are deterministic given the same vocabulary and the same accepted Rosetta set, the neural path is not used for an action the symbolic interface can complete, tool improvements accepted from the neural path are reduced to sequential integers, and training a model is not a substitute for tool improvement inside the harness. Translation that only maps language runs, without a harness, is unchanged. Clause 4.7 item 7 keeps Clause 4.4 neural proposals optional and distinct." },
  { number := 278, text := "" },
  { number := 279, text := "The cultural marker in Clause 1.3 is not a conformance item." },
  { number := 280, text := "" },
  { number := 281, text := "Optional neural proposals (Clause 4.4 item 1), optional Systems Lean formalization of fragments (Clause 4.3 item 5), and optional natural language translation (Clause 4.5 item 1) are not required for conformance when absent. When they are present, the MUST clauses that apply to them in Clause 5 items 3 and 4 still hold. Clause 5 item 6 applies if and only if the product claims the neurosymbolic harness interface." },
  { number := 282, text := "" },
  { number := 283, text := "This specification is not itself a conforming implementation. Meeting these items is a claim about a product, not about this markdown file. This document does not claim that a neurosymbolic harness exists." },
  { number := 284, text := "" },
  { number := 285, text := "## 6. Residual" },
  { number := 286, text := "" },
  { number := 287, text := "This section is normative for residual honesty of this document. It does not add product behavior beyond Clauses 4 and 5. Silence about an unpublished specification, an unassigned number, an unnumbered substrate, an unimplemented requirement, or an optional path named in this document is nonconforming for this specification as a document. A parenthetical planned file name in Scope is not the residual record. The repository root `RESIDUAL.md` restates residual for the numbered specification program; this clause is the residual record for this specification." },
  { number := 288, text := "" },
  { number := 289, text := "### 6.1 Unpublished specifications and unassigned numbers" },
  { number := 290, text := "" },
  { number := 291, text := "1. fargo has no assigned specification number. A previous plan that assigned number 0005 to fargo is withdrawn. Number 0005 is Concise American Technical English (`0005_CATE.md`). Number 0006 is Recursive Self Improvement (`0006_RSI.md`). This document does not invent a new number for fargo. This document does not require fargo." },
  { number := 292, text := "2. The Carbonado Network Protocol has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. Discussion has mentioned 0006 as a possible later number. That mention is not an assignment. This document does not create a file for it." },
  { number := 293, text := "" },
  { number := 294, text := "### 6.2 Lean Machine numbered as 0013" },
  { number := 295, text := "" },
  { number := 296, text := "1. Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`. That document is specification 0013. This document MUST NOT be read as restating Lean Machine or as assigning Legal Lean or Holy Lean a separate number. Neurosymbolic integration remains in this document." },
  { number := 297, text := "" },
  { number := 298, text := "### 6.3 Product tree pins versus this repository's `ref/`" },
  { number := 299, text := "" },
  { number := 300, text := "1. `0000_spec.md` Clause 12 binds external specifications this specifications repository cites to `ref/` in this repository." },
  { number := 301, text := "2. Lean 4, Idris 2, CompCert, and Rust are cited by [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) as Form 1 pins of the Systems Lean product tree, not of this specifications repository's `ref/`. This document does not move those pins here." },
  { number := 302, text := "3. There is no SSSSS product tree pin in this repository. SSSSS is a real product. The work is incomplete, ongoing, and is not ready for use. This document MUST NOT be read as claiming that SSSSS never started or does not exist." },
  { number := 303, text := "4. beastdb is specified in this repository as `0003_beastdb.md`. That numbered specification is not a `ref/` pin of an upstream store." },
  { number := 304, text := "" },
  { number := 305, text := "### 6.4 Product requirements that are not ready for use" },
  { number := 306, text := "" },
  { number := 307, text := "This document specifies SSSSS. SSSSS is a real product. The work is incomplete, ongoing, and is not ready for use. It MUST NOT be read as claiming that SSSSS never started or does not exist. Claiming that SSSSS never started is Cons False in the SSSSS proofs module. Claiming that SSSSS is ready for use is Cons False in that same module. The following are requirements in Clause 4, not done work:" },
  { number := 308, text := "" },
  { number := 309, text := "1. Encoding as sequential language runs with a `LanguageID` prefix only on change is a requirement. Sequential identity of those runs is not a claim that a store already assigns sequential integers. This document does not claim those runs are implemented." },
  { number := 310, text := "2. Sequential `LanguageID` and sequential `WordID` are primary identity. The hashing ban is a requirement in Clause 4.1 item 5. That ban is not a proof that an engine already obeys it. Treating the hashing ban as proof that an engine already uses sequential identity is Cons False in the SSSSS proofs module. An auxiliary digest that replaces sequential stored identity is already Cons False in that module. Do not wrap that `Bool` a second time. SSSSS remains ongoing and is not ready for use." },
  { number := 311, text := "3. Combined capacity `2^64` languages times `2^64` `WordID` values is a requirement. This document does not claim that capacity is implemented." },
  { number := 312, text := "4. Rosetta relations with `RelationType` and provenance tags are a requirement. This document does not claim a Rosetta store is implemented." },
  { number := 313, text := "5. A deterministic pipeline given the same vocabulary and relation set, including ingest, tokenize, vocabulary lookup or insert, intermediate representation, and emit by inverse lookup, is a requirement. This document does not claim a pipeline is implemented." },
  { number := 314, text := "6. Failure or a named hole when no accepted mapping exists, without inventing hash identity, is a requirement. This document does not claim that emit path is implemented." },
  { number := 315, text := "7. Reduction of any accepted neural proposal to sequential integers is a requirement. This document does not claim a neural proposer exists." },
  { number := 316, text := "8. Provisional marking of natural language translation unless Lean proven or high confidence is a requirement when that translation is offered. This document does not claim a natural language translator exists." },
  { number := 317, text := "9. Durable state in `beastdb` is a requirement. This document does not claim an SSSSS backed by `beastdb` is implemented." },
  { number := 318, text := "10. A Systems Lean core that can target the freestanding Slake path for components that are safety critical, that run in environments with tight resources, and that are freestanding, with CompCert verified compilation and a bootstrapped Slake that fully typechecks as required by Clause 4.6. Residual honesty does not substitute for those validation steps. Those steps remain requirements. They are not claimed done." },
  { number := 319, text := "11. Neurosymbolic integration as specified in Clause 4.7, including a symbolic interface in Systems Lean, a neural path used only when that interface cannot complete the action, tool improvements reduced to sequential integers, and a ban on substituting model training for tool improvement inside the harness. That integration is specified. It is not a shipped product. Claiming the harness is a distinct claim from optional neural proposals. Treating that specified harness as a shipped product is Cons False in the SSSSS proofs module. A claimed harness that spends neural work when the symbolic interface can complete the action is already Cons False in that module. Do not wrap that `Bool` a second time. SSSSS remains ongoing and is not ready for use." },
  { number := 320, text := "" },
  { number := 321, text := "### 6.5 Informative and optional items this document names" },
  { number := 322, text := "" },
  { number := 323, text := "1. The Rick and Morty cultural marker (Clause 1.3) is informative. Television canon is not a conformance item." },
  { number := 324, text := "2. Neural proposals are MAY (Clause 4.4). Lean proving a neural proposal before it becomes authoritative for semantics or behavior that is safety critical is SHOULD, not MUST." },
  { number := 325, text := "3. Natural language translation is MAY, best effort, and provisional unless proven or high confidence (Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 326, text := "4. Formalizing fragments into Systems Lean is MAY (Clause 4.3 item 5)." },
  { number := 327, text := "5. An auxiliary hash index is allowed only as an index that is not primary (Clause 4.1 item 5)." },
  { number := 328, text := "6. Model Context Protocol and Agent Client Protocol MAY be named as other wires (Clause 4.7.1). This specification does not forbid them and does not require them." },
  { number := 329, text := "7. Neural proposals remain MAY (Clause 4.4). Claiming the neurosymbolic harness interface is a distinct claim (Clause 4.7)." },
  { number := 330, text := "" },
  { number := 331, text := "### 6.6 Neurosymbolic integration is specified and is not shipped" },
  { number := 332, text := "" },
  { number := 333, text := "The neurosymbolic integration in Clause 4.7 is specified in this document. It is not a shipped product. SSSSS is a real product. The work is incomplete, ongoing, and is not ready for use. This document MUST NOT be read as claiming that SSSSS never started or does not exist. This document MUST NOT be read as claiming that a conforming neurosymbolic harness exists. Treating that specified harness as a shipped product is Cons False in the SSSSS proofs module." },
  { number := 334, text := "" },
  { number := 335, text := "## 7. Changelog" },
  { number := 336, text := "" },
  { number := 337, text := "### 0.1.0 - 20260831" },
  { number := 338, text := "" },
  { number := 339, text := "Current version line is 0.1.0 by operator order. Changelog history records that a 1.0.0 line existed as unpublished working text." },
  { number := 340, text := "" },
  { number := 341, text := "Adds neurosymbolic integration as Clause 4.7 with definitions of harness, symbolic interface, neural path, tool improvement call, and neurosymbolic combination. When a product claims that harness interface, it MUST expose the symbolic interface as an alternative deterministic interface, implement that interface in Systems Lean, keep recipe lookup and emit deterministic given the same vocabulary and Rosetta set, MUST NOT use the neural path for an action the symbolic interface can complete, MUST reduce tool improvements to sequential integers before acceptance, and MUST NOT substitute training a model for tool improvement inside the harness. Model Context Protocol and Agent Client Protocol MAY be named as other wires and are not forbidden. Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`. The integration is specified and is not a shipped product. SSSSS is a real product. The work is incomplete and is not ready for use. Clause 6.4 records sequential identity and the hashing ban as requirements, not as proof that an engine already obeys them. Treating the hashing ban as that proof is Cons False. Treating the specified neurosymbolic harness as a shipped product is Cons False. This document does not invent a number for fargo." },
  { number := 342, text := "" },
  { number := 343, text := "### 1.0.0 - 20260824" },
  { number := 344, text := "" },
  { number := 345, text := "First publication of this specification text. Defines SSSSS as specification 0004 with file name `0004_SSSSS.md`; requires sequential language runs with LanguageID prefix only on change; requires 64 bit sequential LanguageID and per language sequential WordID as primary identity and forbids hashing as primary identity; states combined capacity `2^64` languages times `2^64` WordIDs; requires Rosetta relations with RelationType and provenance `neural-proposed`, `human-confirmed`, or `Lean-proven`; requires a deterministic pipeline given the same vocabulary and relation set; permits neural proposals only after reduction to sequential integers; permits natural language translation as best effort work that MUST be marked provisional unless Lean proven or high confidence; requires durable state in beastdb as specified in `0003_beastdb.md`; requires a Systems Lean core as specified in `0002_Systems_Lean.md`; and requires CompCert verified compilation and a bootstrapped Slake that fully typechecks for SSSSS components that are safety critical, that run in environments with tight resources, and that are freestanding, with residual honesty not substituting for those steps." },
  { number := 346, text := "" },
  { number := 347, text := "This 1.0.0 also records: this document does not claim a conforming implementation exists; Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`; fargo has no assigned specification number and is not required here; Recursive Self Improvement is specified in `0006_RSI.md`; the Carbonado Network Protocol has no assigned number; the five consecutive S letters are an informative cultural marker and not a conformance item." },
  { number := 348, text := "" },
  { number := 349, text := "This unpublished 1.0.0 also records that hyphenated modifiers in prose were rephrased into ordinary English. Deleting the hyphen and leaving the same two words is not enough." },
  { number := 350, text := "" },
  { number := 351, text := "This unpublished 1.0.0 also records that citations of Keagan McLelland (Proof of Keags) research SHALL keep the publisher links on those pages (back linking)." },
  { number := 352, text := "" },
  { number := 353, text := "No prior public release of this specification exists." },
  { number := 354, text := "" },
  { number := 355, text := "## 8. Copyright" },
  { number := 356, text := "" },
  { number := 357, text := "This work is released into the public domain under the Unlicense as specified in `0009_PDOSS.md`. Anyone is free to copy, modify, publish, use, compile, sell, or distribute this specification, either in source code form or as a compiled binary, for any purpose, commercial or noncommercial, and by any means. See `UNLICENSE.md` in this repository. Novel SSSSS source, when it exists, is likewise Unlicensed. Upstream components retain their original licenses." },
  { number := 358, text := "" },
  { number := 359, text := "## 9. Acknowledgments" },
  { number := 360, text := "" },
  { number := 361, text := "Author: Hunter \"cryptoquick\" Beast." },
  { number := 362, text := "" },
  { number := 363, text := "This work is significantly inspired by the research and public talks of Keagan McLelland (Proof of Keags), particularly:" },
  { number := 364, text := "" },
  { number := 365, text := "1. Formal Vibefication (2026-05-12) - https://proofofkeags.com/research/2026-05-12-formal-vibefication.html" },
  { number := 366, text := "2. Taking \"Don't Trust. Verify.\" Seriously (2026-07-20) - https://proofofkeags.com/research/2026-07-20-taking-dont-trust-verify-seriously.html" },
  { number := 367, text := "3. Formal Verification of Bitcoin BitDevs talk (2026-07-14) - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E0VjopN2sgg" },
  { number := 368, text := "" },
  { number := 369, text := "Those pages and that talk are research and presentation. They are not external specifications under `0000_spec.md` Clause 12. Citations of this work SHALL keep those publisher links (back linking)." },
  { number := 370, text := "" },
